{"type":"new","contents":"import Mathlib.Algebra.Star.Basic\nimport Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic\nimport Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.DrazinDilationGap\n\nTheorem-safe carrier for the distinction between:\n\n* Drazin regular support `P_D = A * Aᴰ`;\n* Drazin defect support `Q0 = 1 - P_D`;\n* Moore-Penrose range/domain supports;\n* dilation gap `G = c • (P_range - P_domain)`;\n* algebraic Drazin supercharge `Q = 2 • [P_D, G]`;\n* witness-gated kinetic/defect split of `Q²`.\n\nThis file deliberately does not identify the dilation gap with the singular\nsector.  The singular sector is `Q0`; the gap is the Moore-Penrose support\nmismatch.\n-/\n\nnoncomputable section\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.DrazinDilationGap\n\n/-- Generic commutator. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ndef commutator {Op : Type*} [Mul Op] [Sub Op] (X Y : Op) : Op :=\n  X * Y - Y * X\n\n/--\nDrazin support data for an operator `A`.\n\n`P_D` is the regular Drazin support. `Q0` is the defect/generalized-zero sector.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nstructure DrazinData (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] [Star Op] where\n  A : Op\n  AD : Op\n  P_D : Op\n  Q0 : Op\n  P_D_def : P_D = A * AD\n  commute : A * AD = AD * A\n  P_D_idempotent : P_D * P_D = P_D\n  P_D_self_adjoint : star P_D = P_D\n  Q0_def : Q0 = 1 - P_D\n\nnamespace DrazinData\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] [Star Op] (D : DrazinData Op)\n\n/-- Readback: the Drazin defect support is the complement of the regular support. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem defectSupport_eq_one_sub_regularSupport :\n    D.Q0 = 1 - D.P_D :=\n  D.Q0_def\n\nend DrazinData\n\n/--\nMoore-Penrose support data.\n\n`P_range` is the output/range support; `P_domain` is the input/domain support.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nstructure MoorePenroseSupportData (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] [Star Op] where\n  A : Op\n  A_MP : Op\n  P_range : Op\n  P_domain : Op\n  P_range_def : P_range = A * A_MP\n  P_domain_def : P_domain = A_MP * A\n  P_range_idempotent : P_range * P_range = P_range\n  P_domain_idempotent : P_domain * P_domain = P_domain\n  P_range_self_adjoint : star P_range = P_range\n  P_domain_self_adjoint : star P_domain = P_domain\n\n/--\nDilation gap data.\n\nUsually `halfScalar = 1 / 2`; it is kept as a field so this socket can be used\nwith abstract carriers where a literal inverse of `2` is not the right API.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nstructure DilationGapData (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] [Star Op] [SMul ℝ Op] where\n  mp : MoorePenroseSupportData Op\n  halfScalar : ℝ\n  G : Op\n  G_def : G = halfScalar • (mp.P_range - mp.P_domain)\n\nnamespace DilationGapData\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] [Star Op] [SMul ℝ Op] (G : DilationGapData Op)\n\n/-- Readback: the dilation gap is a scaled Moore-Penrose range/domain mismatch. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem eq_scaled_range_sub_domain :\n    G.G = G.halfScalar • (G.mp.P_range - G.mp.P_domain) :=\n  G.G_def\n\n/--\nIf the Moore-Penrose range and domain supports agree, the dilation gap vanishes.\n\nThe zero-smul law is passed explicitly because this socket assumes only\n`SMul ℝ Op`, not a stronger module interface.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem eq_zero_of_supports_equal\n    (hSupport : G.mp.P_range = G.mp.P_domain)\n    (hzero : G.halfScalar • (0 : Op) = 0) :\n    G.G = 0 := by\n  simpa [G.G_def, hSupport] using hzero\n\nend DilationGapData\n\n/--\nAlgebraic Drazin supercharge.\n\nThis is the real/algebraic odd generator `Q_alg = 2 • [P_D, G]`.  A complex\nHilbert self-adjoint version can insert the conventional factor `i` in a richer\ncarrier.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nstructure DrazinSuperchargeData (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] [Star Op] [SMul ℝ Op] where\n  drazin : DrazinData Op\n  gap : DilationGapData Op\n  Q_alg : Op\n  Q_alg_def : Q_alg = (2 : ℝ) • commutator drazin.P_D gap.G\n\nnamespace DrazinSuperchargeData\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] [Star Op] [SMul ℝ Op] (Q : DrazinSuperchargeData Op)\n\n/-- Readback: the algebraic supercharge is generated by the Drazin support/gap commutator. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem eq_two_smul_commutator :\n    Q.Q_alg = (2 : ℝ) • commutator Q.drazin.P_D Q.gap.G :=\n  Q.Q_alg_def\n\nend DrazinSuperchargeData\n\n/--\nKinetic/defect split of the squared Drazin supercharge.\n\nThis is witness-gated: the split is not asserted for arbitrary carriers unless\nthe required structural laws are supplied.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nstructure DrazinKineticDefectSplit (Op : Type*) [Ring Op] [Star Op] [SMul ℝ Op] where\n  supercharge : DrazinSuperchargeData Op\n  H_kin : Op\n  Z_defect : Op\n  split_law : supercharge.Q_alg * supercharge.Q_alg = H_kin + Z_defect\n  H_kin_regular :\n    supercharge.drazin.P_D * H_kin * supercharge.drazin.P_D = H_kin\n  Z_defect_supported :\n    supercharge.drazin.Q0 * Z_defect * supercharge.drazin.Q0 = Z_defect\n\nnamespace DrazinKineticDefectSplit\n\nvariable {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] [Star Op] [SMul ℝ Op] (S : DrazinKineticDefectSplit Op)\n\n/-- The square of the Drazin supercharge decomposes into kinetic and defect shadows. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem supercharge_square_split :\n    S.supercharge.Q_alg * S.supercharge.Q_alg = S.H_kin + S.Z_defect :=\n  S.split_law\n\n/-- Readback: the kinetic summand is supported on the Drazin regular support. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem kinetic_regular_support :\n    S.supercharge.drazin.P_D * S.H_kin * S.supercharge.drazin.P_D = S.H_kin :=\n  S.H_kin_regular\n\n/-- Readback: the defect summand is supported on the Drazin defect support. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem defect_supported :\n    S.supercharge.drazin.Q0 * S.Z_defect * S.supercharge.drazin.Q0 = S.Z_defect :=\n  S.Z_defect_supported\n\nend DrazinKineticDefectSplit\n\n/--\nIf two self-adjoint operators generate a commutator, that commutator is\nskew-adjoint.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem star_commutator_eq_neg_of_self_adjoint\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] [StarRing Op] {P G : Op}\n    (hP : star P = P) (hG : star G = G) :\n    star (commutator P G) = -commutator P G := by\n  simp [commutator, hP, hG]\n  noncomm_ring\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.DrazinDilationGap\n\n","mtime":1778819962686}